-- title:
--   Two ideals at one split place span a free rank-two lattice
-- statement:
--   Let $c,d\in\mathbb Q$, let $q$ be a prime, and assume $H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,c,d]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $q$: $c<0$, $d<0$, and for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ every nonzero element of $H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ is a unit if and only if $q\in w$. Let $O\subseteq H$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. $1\in O$, $O$ is closed under multiplication, $O$ spans $H$ over $\mathbb Q$, $O$ is finitely generated, and every order containing $O$ equals $O$. Let $r\neq q$ be a prime and $v$ a height-one prime with $r\in v$. Let $g_1,g_2$ be units of $H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A^{f}_{\mathbb Q}$ whose component under the evaluation $H\otimes\mathbb A^f\to H\otimes\mathbb Q_w$ is $1$ for every $w\neq v$. Assume: for every ring isomorphism $\varphi\colon H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v\cong M_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ with $\varphi(1\otimes t)=t\cdot 1$ for all $t\in\mathbb Q_v$ and with $x$ lying in the additive group generated by the $z\otimes c$ ($z\in O$, $c\in\mathbb Z_v$) if and only if all entries $\varphi(x)_{ij}$ are in $\mathbb Z_v$, both $\det\varphi\bigl((g_1g_2)_v\bigr)$ and $\det\varphi\bigl((g_1g_2)^{-1}_v\bigr)$ lie in $\mathbb Z_v$. Then there are $\gamma,\gamma'\in M_2(H)$ with $\gamma\gamma'=\gamma'\gamma=1$ such that for every $x=(x_0,x_1)\in H^2$ all coordinates of $\gamma' x$ lie in $O$ if and only if $x_0\in\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,O\,g_1$ and $x_1\in\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,O\,g_2$, where $\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,O\,g$ is the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $z\in H$ with $z\otimes 1\in g\cdot\mathrm{finiteAdeleBox}\,O$, the latter being the additive group generated by the $z\otimes a$ with $z\in O$ and $a$ an integral finite adele.
--
--   This is the case, supported at a single split auxiliary place, of the classical statement that a rank-two locally free right module over a maximal order in a definite rational quaternion algebra is free — equivalently that $M_2(O)$ has class number one, in the line of Eichler, Swan and Fröhlich. It is used by [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_matrix_forall_mulVec_mem_iff_of_le`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_matrix_forall_mulVec_mem_iff_of_le), where the general pair of right ideals is moved within its class to this situation.
